From c4946a89960ba6179709eabe71224c7ded63eb6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 21:56:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] terminus: add refreshFirmwareParameters method

Add `refreshFirmwareParameters` to query firmware parameters without
running `handleMctpEndpoints`.

After the OS is ready, if the PLDM device version information needs
to be queried. However, using handleMctpEndpoints for this purpose
may be risky, because it re-initializes MCTP endpoints while the
PLDM bus may already be busy with other traffic. This may affect
firmware updates and increase bus contention. Since only the
firmware parameters are needed, add refreshFirmwareParameters to
query them directly without rerunning handleMctpEndpoints.

`getFirmwareParameters` requires `descriptorMap` to be available. If
`descriptorMap` does not exist yet, send
`sendQueryDeviceIdentifiersRequest` first to populate it. The retry
mechanism then automatically re-triggers
`refreshFirmwareParameters` to read the version information.

If reading firmware parameters fails, the same retry mechanism is
triggered automatically.

The link of the gerrit:
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/90018

Signed-off-by: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
